        'Adventure', 'The Lamkhaga Pass Trek is one of the most breathtaking Himalayan journeys situated across the mesmerizing landscapes of UTTARKAHSI, Uttrakhand. Rising to an impressive altitude of 17329ft over a duration of 11D/10N, this expedition offers a transcendent blend of ancient cultural lore, sacred alpine sanctuaries, and pristine high-altitude wilderness.

Traversing through dense oak, pine, and vibrant rhododendron canopies, travelers experience panoramic vistas of snow-crowned Himalayan peaks, sparkling glacial river valleys, and remote mountain hamlets steeped in centuries-old traditions. The journey commences from Dehradun, taking explorers deep into untamed valleys where high altitude pass, snow possible graces the trails. Each step along this route reveals untouched flora, alpine meadows, and timeless folklore cherished by the local indigenous communities.

Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Lamkhaga Pass Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.', 'The Lamkhaga Pass Trek is one of the most breathtaking Himalayan journeys situated across the mesmerizing landscapes of UTTARKAHSI, Uttrakhand. Rising to an impressive altitude of 17329ft over a duration of 11D/10N, this expedition offers a transcendent blend of ancient cultural lore, sacred alpine sanctuaries, and pristine high-altitude wilderness.

Traversing through dense oak, pine, and vibrant rhododendron canopies, travelers experience panoramic vistas of snow-crowned Himalayan peaks, sparkling glacial river valleys, and remote mountain hamlets steeped in centuries-old traditions. The journey commences from Dehradun, taking explorers deep into untamed valleys where high altitude pass, snow possible graces the trails. Each step along this route reveals untouched flora, alpine meadows, and timeless folklore cherished by the local indigenous communities.

Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Lamkhaga Pass Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.',
        '[{"day": 1, "title": "Dehradun to Harsil", "description": "Day 1: Dehradun to Harsil (8,595 ft) \u2013 Drive 240 km in about 9\u201310 hours through Mussoorie, Uttarkashi and the Bhagirathi Valley to reach Harsil. Enjoy beautiful mountain views, apple orchards and riverside landscapes before checking into the campsite or guesthouse for overnight stay and trek briefing.", "distance": "240 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 2, "title": "Harsil to Kyarkoti", "description": "Day 2: Harsil to Kyarkoti (12,600 ft) \u2013 Trek approximately 14 km in 6\u20137 hours through dense pine, deodar and birch forests alongside the Jalandhari Gad stream. The trail gradually ascends into alpine meadows with magnificent views of snow-covered peaks before reaching the scenic campsite at Kyarkoti.", "distance": "14 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 3, "title": "Kyarkoti to Lamkhaga Base Camp", "description": "Day 3: Kyarkoti to Lamkhaga Base Camp (14,500 ft) \u2013 Cover around 12 km in 6\u20137 hours across meadows, rocky terrain, glacial moraine and mountain streams. The landscape becomes more rugged as you gain altitude, offering spectacular views of surrounding Himalayan ranges before camping at Lamkhaga Base Camp.", "distance": "12 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 4, "title": "Acclimatization at Lamkhaga Base Camp", "description": "Day 4: Acclimatization at Lamkhaga Base Camp (14,500 ft) \u2013 Spend the day acclimatizing to the high altitude with short exploratory hikes around the glacier region and nearby ridges. This rest day helps the body adapt to reduced oxygen levels and prepares trekkers for the demanding pass crossing ahead.", "distance": "", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 5, "title": "Lamkhaga Base Camp to Gundar via Lamkhaga Pass", "description": "Day 5: Lamkhaga Base Camp to Gundar via Lamkhaga Pass (17,330 ft) \u2013 Trek nearly 13 km in 9\u201310 hours, crossing the majestic Lamkhaga Pass, the highest point of the expedition. Traverse snowfields, glaciers and steep sections while enjoying breathtaking panoramic views before descending to the campsite at Gundar (15,250 ft).", "distance": "13 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 6, "title": "Gundar", "description": "Day 6: Gundar (15,250 ft) to Dumti (13,240 ft) \u2013 Descend approximately 15 km in 6\u20137 hours through rugged valleys, rocky landscapes and glacial terrain. The trail gradually enters greener surroundings with streams and alpine vegetation before reaching the campsite at Dumti.", "distance": "15 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 7, "title": "Dumti to Rani Kanda", "description": "Day 7: Dumti to Rani Kanda (12,070 ft) \u2013 Trek around 9 km in 4\u20135 hours through beautiful alpine meadows, grazing fields and open valleys. The gradual descent offers stunning views of the Baspa Valley and surrounding mountains before arriving at the picturesque campsite of Rani Kanda.", "distance": "9 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 8, "title": "Rani Kanda to Chitkul", "description": "Day 8: Rani Kanda to Chitkul (11,320 ft) \u2013 Cover about 9 km in 4\u20135 hours descending through meadows and traditional shepherd trails to reach Chitkul, the last inhabited village of the Baspa Valley. Explore its charming wooden houses, local culture and scenic surroundings before overnight stay.", "distance": "9 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 9, "title": "Chitkul", "description": "Day 9: Chitkul (11,320 ft) to Sangla (8,890 ft) \u2013 Drive nearly 25 km in 1\u20132 hours along the Baspa River to Sangla. Spend the day exploring the beautiful valley, traditional villages and apple orchards while relaxing after completing the trekking section.", "distance": "25 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 10, "title": "Sangla to Shimla", "description": "Day 10: Sangla to Shimla (7,220 ft) \u2013 Drive approximately 220 km in 8\u20139 hours through the scenic Kinnaur region and Sutlej Valley. Enjoy changing landscapes from high mountains to pine forests before reaching Shimla for an overnight stay.", "distance": "220 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 11, "title": "Shimla to Chandigarh/Dehradun", "description": "Day 11: Shimla to Chandigarh/Dehradun \u2013 After breakfast, depart for Chandigarh or Dehradun, bringing the adventurous 11-day Lamkhaga Pass Trek to a memorable conclusion.", "distance": "", "time": "", "image": ""}]'::jsonb, '[{"location": "Airport: Jolly Grant Airport", "price": 0}, {"location": "Railway: Dehradun Railway Station", "price": 0}, {"location": "Base: Dehradun", "price": 0}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb,
