Traversing through dense oak, pine, and vibrant rhododendron canopies, travelers experience panoramic vistas of snow-crowned Himalayan peaks, sparkling glacial river valleys, and remote mountain hamlets steeped in centuries-old traditions. The journey commences from Dehradun, taking explorers deep into untamed valleys where glaciated terrain, harsh conditions graces the trails. Each step along this route reveals untouched flora, alpine meadows, and timeless folklore cherished by the local indigenous communities.

Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Auden'' Col Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.', 'The Auden'' Col Trek is one of the most breathtaking Himalayan journeys situated across the mesmerizing landscapes of UTTARKAHSI, Uttrakhand. Rising to an impressive altitude of 18012ft over a duration of 16D/15N, this expedition offers a transcendent blend of ancient cultural lore, sacred alpine sanctuaries, and pristine high-altitude wilderness.

Traversing through dense oak, pine, and vibrant rhododendron canopies, travelers experience panoramic vistas of snow-crowned Himalayan peaks, sparkling glacial river valleys, and remote mountain hamlets steeped in centuries-old traditions. The journey commences from Dehradun, taking explorers deep into untamed valleys where glaciated terrain, harsh conditions graces the trails. Each step along this route reveals untouched flora, alpine meadows, and timeless folklore cherished by the local indigenous communities.

Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Auden'' Col Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.',
        '[{"day": 1, "title": "Dehradun to Gangotri", "description": "Day 1: Dehradun to Gangotri (10,200 ft) \u2013 Drive approximately 250 km in 9\u201310 hours via Uttarkashi and Harsil to reach Gangotri. Enjoy scenic views of the Bhagirathi River valley, pine forests and Himalayan peaks before an overnight stay and trek briefing.", "distance": "250 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 2, "title": "Gangotri to Nala Camp", "description": "Day 2: Gangotri to Nala Camp (12,140 ft) \u2013 Trek around 12 km in 5\u20136 hours along the Bhagirathi River through forests and alpine terrain. The gradual ascent provides excellent acclimatization before reaching Nala Camp.", "distance": "12 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 3, "title": "Nala Camp to Rudugaira Base Camp", "description": "Day 3: Nala Camp to Rudugaira Base Camp (14,100 ft) \u2013 Cover nearly 10 km in 5\u20136 hours through meadows, moraine fields and rocky landscapes. The trail offers stunning views of the Rudugaira Valley and surrounding snow-clad peaks.", "distance": "10 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 4, "title": "Acclimatization Day at Rudugaira Base Camp", "description": "Day 4: Acclimatization Day at Rudugaira Base Camp (14,100 ft) \u2013 Spend the day acclimatizing with short hikes and glacier exploration around the campsite. Proper acclimatization is essential before entering higher glacial terrain.", "distance": "", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 5, "title": "Rudugaira Base Camp to Gangotri Group Base Camp", "description": "Day 5: Rudugaira Base Camp to Gangotri Group Base Camp (15,420 ft) \u2013 Trek approximately 8 km in 5\u20136 hours over moraine and glacial sections. The terrain becomes increasingly rugged as you approach the higher reaches of the expedition.", "distance": "8 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 6, "title": "Gangotri Group Base Camp to Upper Camp", "description": "Day 6: Gangotri Group Base Camp to Upper Camp (16,400 ft) \u2013 Cover around 6 km in 4\u20135 hours across glaciers, boulder fields and snow patches. Reach Upper Camp and prepare for the upcoming pass crossing.", "distance": "6 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 7, "title": "Acclimatization and Technical Training at Upper Camp", "description": "Day 7: Acclimatization and Technical Training at Upper Camp (16,400 ft) \u2013 Spend the day practicing rope techniques, glacier travel and ice walking while allowing the body to adjust to the altitude.", "distance": "", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 8, "title": "Upper Camp to Auden''s Col Base Camp", "description": "Day 8: Upper Camp to Auden''s Col Base Camp (17,060 ft) \u2013 Trek approximately 5 km in 4\u20135 hours through challenging glacier terrain and crevassed sections before reaching the base camp below the pass.", "distance": "5 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 9, "title": "Day 9", "description": "Day 9: Auden''s Col Base Camp to Khatling Glacier Camp via Auden''s Col (18,010 ft) \u2013 Trek nearly 12 km in 10\u201312 hours crossing the magnificent Auden''s Col, the highest point of the trek. Traverse steep snow slopes, glaciers and technical sections before descending to Khatling Glacier Camp.", "distance": "12 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 10, "title": "Khatling Glacier Camp to Zero Point", "description": "Day 10: Khatling Glacier Camp to Zero Point (15,750 ft) \u2013 Cover around 10 km in 6\u20137 hours descending through glacial moraine and rugged landscapes. Enjoy spectacular views of surrounding Himalayan peaks.", "distance": "10 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 11, "title": "Zero Point to Waterfall Camp", "description": "Day 11: Zero Point to Waterfall Camp (13,780 ft) \u2013 Trek approximately 12 km in 6\u20137 hours through alpine valleys, rocky trails and streams before reaching the campsite near a beautiful waterfall.", "distance": "12 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 12, "title": "Waterfall Camp to Chowki", "description": "Day 12: Waterfall Camp to Chowki (11,800 ft) \u2013 Descend nearly 14 km in 6\u20137 hours through dense forests and meadows. The trail gradually becomes greener as altitude decreases.", "distance": "14 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 13, "title": "Chowki to Masar Tal", "description": "Day 13: Chowki to Masar Tal (10,990 ft) \u2013 Trek around 10 km in 5\u20136 hours through scenic valleys and forest sections before arriving at the serene campsite near Masar Tal.", "distance": "10 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 14, "title": "Masar Tal to Gangi Village", "description": "Day 14: Masar Tal to Gangi Village (8,300 ft) \u2013 Cover approximately 12 km in 5\u20136 hours descending through traditional shepherd trails and beautiful mountain landscapes to reach Gangi Village.", "distance": "12 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 15, "title": "Gangi to Ghuttu and Drive to Uttarkashi", "description": "Day 15: Gangi to Ghuttu and Drive to Uttarkashi (3,790 ft) \u2013 Trek about 8 km in 3\u20134 hours to Ghuttu, followed by a drive of 5\u20136 hours to Uttarkashi for an overnight stay.", "distance": "8 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 16, "title": "Uttarkashi to Dehradun", "description": "Day 16: Uttarkashi to Dehradun \u2013 Drive approximately 170 km in 6\u20137 hours along the Bhagirathi Valley to Dehradun, concluding one of the most technical and challenging Himalayan expeditions.", "distance": "170 km", "time": "", "image": ""}]'::jsonb, '[{"location": "Airport: Jolly Grant Airport", "price": 0}, {"location": "Railway: Dehradun Railway Station", "price": 0}, {"location": "Base: Dehradun", "price": 0}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb,
        30.7333, 76.7794, '18012ft', '', '',
        '{"Ideal Season": "JUNE, SEP, OCT | Temp: -15\u2103'' to 10\u2103'' | Weather: Glaciated terrain, harsh conditions"}'::jsonb, 'JUNE, SEP, OCT', '539 km', 'Dehradun', 'Gangotri',
        'Jolly Grant Airport', 'Dehradun Railway Station', 'YES', '9843ft', '18012ft',
        '-15℃''', '10℃''', 'Glaciated terrain, harsh conditions', 'Uttrakhand', 'UTTARKAHSI',
        'TREK', 5.0
    ) RETURNING id INTO tid;
