Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Borasu Pass Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.',
        '[{"day": 1, "title": "Dehradun to Sankri", "description": "Day 1: Dehradun to Sankri (6,400 ft) \u2013 Drive approximately 200 km in 8\u20139 hours via Mussoorie, Purola and Mori to reach Sankri. The scenic journey passes through pine forests, riverside villages and mountain valleys before an overnight stay and trek briefing.", "distance": "200 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 2, "title": "Sankri to Seema via Taluka", "description": "Day 2: Sankri to Seema via Taluka (8,200 ft) \u2013 Drive 12 km to Taluka and trek approximately 14 km in 6\u20137 hours along the Supin River through dense forests, wooden bridges and traditional villages to reach Seema, a beautiful campsite near the river.", "distance": "14 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 3, "title": "Seema to Har Ki Dun", "description": "Day 3: Seema to Har Ki Dun (11,700 ft) \u2013 Trek around 12 km in 5\u20136 hours through alpine meadows, conifer forests and picturesque valleys. Enjoy magnificent views of the Swargarohini massif before reaching the expansive meadows of Har Ki Dun.", "distance": "12 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 4, "title": "Har Ki Dun to Ratta Tho", "description": "Day 4: Har Ki Dun to Ratta Tho (13,800 ft) \u2013 Cover nearly 10 km in 5\u20136 hours through glacial valleys, moraine sections and rugged mountain terrain. The trail gradually ascends towards higher alpine landscapes before camping at Ratta Tho.", "distance": "10 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 5, "title": "Ratta Tho to Borasu Pass", "description": "Day 5: Ratta Tho to Borasu Pass (17,225 ft) and Descend to Bonga (13,450 ft) \u2013 Trek approximately 14 km in 9\u201310 hours across snowfields, glaciers and steep mountain slopes to cross the majestic Borasu Pass, the highest point of the expedition. Descend through rocky terrain to reach the campsite at Bonga.", "distance": "14 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 6, "title": "Bonga to Chitkul", "description": "Day 6: Bonga to Chitkul (11,320 ft) \u2013 Trek around 13 km in 5\u20136 hours descending through alpine meadows, shepherd trails and scenic valleys before arriving at Chitkul, the last inhabited village of the Baspa Valley.", "distance": "13 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 7, "title": "Chitkul to Sangla", "description": "Day 7: Chitkul to Sangla (8,890 ft) \u2013 Drive approximately 25 km in 1\u20132 hours along the Baspa River to Sangla. Spend the day relaxing, exploring traditional Kinnauri villages and enjoying views of the surrounding Himalayan peaks.", "distance": "25 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 8, "title": "Sangla to Shimla", "description": "Day 8: Sangla to Shimla (7,220 ft) \u2013 Drive nearly 220 km in 8\u20139 hours via Rampur and Narkanda to reach Shimla, marking the end of the adventurous Borasu Pass Trek.", "distance": "220 km", "time": "", "image": ""}]'::jsonb, '[{"location": "Airport: Jolly Grant Airport", "price": 0}, {"location": "Railway: Dehradun Railway Station", "price": 0}, {"location": "Base: Dehradun", "price": 0}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb,
