        'Adventure', 'The Hampta Pass & Chandratal Lake Trek is one of the most breathtaking Himalayan journeys situated across the mesmerizing landscapes of KULLU, Himachal Pradesh. Rising to an impressive altitude of 14100ft over a duration of 5D/4N, this expedition offers a transcendent blend of ancient cultural lore, sacred alpine sanctuaries, and pristine high-altitude wilderness.

Traversing through dense oak, pine, and vibrant rhododendron canopies, travelers experience panoramic vistas of snow-crowned Himalayan peaks, sparkling glacial river valleys, and remote mountain hamlets steeped in centuries-old traditions. The journey commences from Manali, taking explorers deep into untamed valleys where pleasant days, cold nights graces the trails. Each step along this route reveals untouched flora, alpine meadows, and timeless folklore cherished by the local indigenous communities.

Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Hampta Pass & Chandratal Lake Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.', 'The Hampta Pass & Chandratal Lake Trek is one of the most breathtaking Himalayan journeys situated across the mesmerizing landscapes of KULLU, Himachal Pradesh. Rising to an impressive altitude of 14100ft over a duration of 5D/4N, this expedition offers a transcendent blend of ancient cultural lore, sacred alpine sanctuaries, and pristine high-altitude wilderness.

Traversing through dense oak, pine, and vibrant rhododendron canopies, travelers experience panoramic vistas of snow-crowned Himalayan peaks, sparkling glacial river valleys, and remote mountain hamlets steeped in centuries-old traditions. The journey commences from Manali, taking explorers deep into untamed valleys where pleasant days, cold nights graces the trails. Each step along this route reveals untouched flora, alpine meadows, and timeless folklore cherished by the local indigenous communities.

Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Hampta Pass & Chandratal Lake Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.',
        '[{"day": 1, "title": "Manali to Jobra", "description": "Day 1: Manali to Jobra \u2013 Trek to Chika (10,100 ft) \u2013 Drive approximately 18 km in 1 hour from Manali to Jobra and begin the trek towards Chika. Cover around 3 km in 2\u20133 hours through dense pine forests, maple trees and beautiful meadows alongside the Rani Nallah stream before reaching the picturesque campsite at Chika. Meals: Dinner | Stay: Camps at Chika.", "distance": "3 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 2, "title": "Chika to Balu Ka Ghera", "description": "Day 2: Chika to Balu Ka Ghera (11,900 ft) \u2013 Trek approximately 8 km in 5\u20136 hours through lush grasslands, river crossings and alpine landscapes. The valley gradually opens up, revealing stunning views of snow-covered peaks and glacial streams before arriving at the campsite at Balu Ka Ghera. Meals: Breakfast & Dinner | Stay: Camps at Balu Ka Ghera.", "distance": "8 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 3, "title": "Balu Ka Ghera", "description": "Day 3: Balu Ka Ghera \u2013 Hampta Pass \u2013 Shea Goru (12,900 ft) \u2013 Cover nearly 9 km in 7\u20138 hours while crossing the magnificent Hampta Pass at 14,100 ft, the highest point of the trek. Witness the dramatic transition from the green Kullu Valley to the barren landscapes of Lahaul before descending to Shea Goru for an overnight stay. Meals: Breakfast & Dinner | Stay: Camps at Shea Goru.", "distance": "9 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 4, "title": "Shea Goru to Chatru", "description": "Day 4: Shea Goru to Chatru \u2013 Chandratal Lake Excursion (14,100 ft) \u2013 Trek around 7 km in 4\u20135 hours to Chatru and later drive towards the mesmerizing Chandratal Lake. Spend time exploring the pristine high-altitude lake surrounded by towering Himalayan peaks before returning to the campsite or camp near Chandratal for an overnight stay. Meals: Breakfast & Dinner | Stay: Camps near Chandratal/Chatru.", "distance": "7 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 5, "title": "Chandratal", "description": "Day 5: Chandratal \u2013 Atal Tunnel \u2013 Manali (6,730 ft) \u2013 After breakfast, drive back to Manali via Batal, Gramphu and the famous Atal Tunnel, covering approximately 115 km in 5\u20136 hours. The journey concludes with unforgettable memories of crossing one of the most scenic Himalayan passes.", "distance": "115 km", "time": "", "image": ""}]'::jsonb, '[{"location": "Airport: Bhuntar Airport kullu manali", "price": 0}, {"location": "Railway: Chandigarh Railway Station", "price": 0}, {"location": "Base: Manali", "price": 0}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb,
        30.7333, 76.7794, '14100ft', '', '',
        '{"Ideal Season": "Jun\u2013Sep | Temp: -5\u2103'' to 18\u2103'' | Weather: Pleasant days, cold nights"}'::jsonb, 'Jun–Sep', '160 km', 'Manali', 'Manali',
        'Bhuntar Airport kullu manali', 'Chandigarh Railway Station', 'yes', '9800ft', '14100ft',
        '-5℃''', '18℃''', 'Pleasant days, cold nights', 'Himachal Pradesh', 'KULLU',
        'TREK', 5.0
    ) RETURNING id INTO tid;
