        'Adventure', 'The Buran Ghati Trek is one of the most breathtaking Himalayan journeys situated across the mesmerizing landscapes of SHIMLA, Himachal Pradesh. Rising to an impressive altitude of 15000ft over a duration of 8D/7N, this expedition offers a transcendent blend of ancient cultural lore, sacred alpine sanctuaries, and pristine high-altitude wilderness.

Traversing through dense oak, pine, and vibrant rhododendron canopies, travelers experience panoramic vistas of snow-crowned Himalayan peaks, sparkling glacial river valleys, and remote mountain hamlets steeped in centuries-old traditions. The journey commences from Shimla, taking explorers deep into untamed valleys where cold, snowy at higher altitude graces the trails. Each step along this route reveals untouched flora, alpine meadows, and timeless folklore cherished by the local indigenous communities.

Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Buran Ghati Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.', 'The Buran Ghati Trek is one of the most breathtaking Himalayan journeys situated across the mesmerizing landscapes of SHIMLA, Himachal Pradesh. Rising to an impressive altitude of 15000ft over a duration of 8D/7N, this expedition offers a transcendent blend of ancient cultural lore, sacred alpine sanctuaries, and pristine high-altitude wilderness.

Traversing through dense oak, pine, and vibrant rhododendron canopies, travelers experience panoramic vistas of snow-crowned Himalayan peaks, sparkling glacial river valleys, and remote mountain hamlets steeped in centuries-old traditions. The journey commences from Shimla, taking explorers deep into untamed valleys where cold, snowy at higher altitude graces the trails. Each step along this route reveals untouched flora, alpine meadows, and timeless folklore cherished by the local indigenous communities.

Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Buran Ghati Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.',
        '[{"day": 1, "title": "Shimla to Janglik", "description": "Day 1: Shimla to Janglik (9,200 ft) \u2013 Drive approximately 150 km in 7\u20138 hours via Rohru and Chirgaon to reach the beautiful village of Janglik, the base camp of the trek. Surrounded by traditional Himachali houses, apple orchards and pine forests, the village offers a perfect introduction to the Pabbar Valley. Meals: Dinner | Stay: Camps/Homestay at Janglik.", "distance": "150 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 2, "title": "Janglik to Dayara Thach", "description": "Day 2: Janglik to Dayara Thach (11,100 ft) \u2013 Trek around 8 km in 5\u20136 hours through dense forests of pine, oak and rhododendron, crossing wooden bridges and lush meadows before reaching the scenic campsite of Dayara Thach. Meals: Breakfast & Dinner | Stay: Camps at Dayara Thach.", "distance": "8 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 3, "title": "Dayara Thach to Litham", "description": "Day 3: Dayara Thach to Litham (11,800 ft) \u2013 Cover approximately 7 km in 4\u20135 hours through expansive alpine meadows, shepherd trails and flower-filled valleys. Enjoy magnificent views of the surrounding Himalayan ranges before arriving at the beautiful campsite of Litham. Meals: Breakfast & Dinner | Stay: Camps at Litham.", "distance": "7 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 4, "title": "Acclimatization and Chandranahan Lake Excursion", "description": "Day 4: Acclimatization and Chandranahan Lake Excursion (13,900 ft) \u2013 Trek around 8 km in 4\u20135 hours to the sacred Chandranahan Lake, believed to be the origin of the Pabbar River. Explore the pristine glacial lake and its surroundings before returning to Litham for an overnight stay. Meals: Breakfast & Dinner | Stay: Camps at Litham.", "distance": "8 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 5, "title": "Litham to Dhunda", "description": "Day 5: Litham to Dhunda (13,300 ft) \u2013 Trek approximately 5 km in 3\u20134 hours through moraine fields, alpine terrain and glacial landscapes to reach Dhunda, the base camp for the Buran Pass crossing. Spend the evening preparing for the summit day. Meals: Breakfast & Dinner | Stay: Camps at Dhunda.", "distance": "5 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 6, "title": "Dhunda", "description": "Day 6: Dhunda \u2013 Buran Pass \u2013 River Camp (12,500 ft) \u2013 Trek nearly 10 km in 8\u20139 hours while crossing the spectacular Buran Pass (15,000 ft). Traverse snow slopes, high ridges and dramatic landscapes before descending towards River Camp for an overnight stay. Meals: Breakfast & Dinner | Stay: Camps at River Camp.", "distance": "10 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 7, "title": "River Camp to Barua Village", "description": "Day 7: River Camp to Barua Village (7,200 ft) \u2013 Descend approximately 8 km in 4\u20135 hours through dense forests, alpine meadows and traditional shepherd trails to reach the picturesque village of Barua in the Kinnaur region. Meals: Breakfast & Dinner | Stay: Homestay/Camps at Barua.", "distance": "8 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 8, "title": "Barua to Shimla", "description": "Day 8: Barua to Shimla \u2013 Drive around 220 km in 8\u20139 hours via Rampur and Narkanda to reach Shimla, concluding the memorable Buran Ghati Trek with unforgettable Himalayan experiences.", "distance": "220 km", "time": "", "image": ""}]'::jsonb, '[{"location": "Airport: Jubbarhatti Airport Shimla", "price": 0}, {"location": "Railway: Shimla Railway Station", "price": 0}, {"location": "Base: Shimla", "price": 0}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb,
        30.7333, 76.7794, '15000ft', '', '',
        '{"Ideal Season": "May\u2013Jun, Sep\u2013Oct | Temp: -8\u2103'' to 18\u2103'' | Weather: Cold, snowy at higher altitude"}'::jsonb, 'May–Jun, Sep–Oct', '416 km', 'Shimla', 'Shimla',
        'Jubbarhatti Airport Shimla', 'Shimla Railway Station', 'yes', '8200ft', '15000ft',
        '-8℃''', '18℃''', 'Cold, snowy at higher altitude', 'Himachal Pradesh', 'SHIMLA',
