        'Adventure', 'The Goechala - Dzongri Trek is one of the most breathtaking Himalayan journeys situated across the mesmerizing landscapes of West Sikkim, Sikkim. Rising to an impressive altitude of 16100 ft over a duration of 11D/10N, this expedition offers a transcendent blend of ancient cultural lore, sacred alpine sanctuaries, and pristine high-altitude wilderness.

Traversing through dense oak, pine, and vibrant rhododendron canopies, travelers experience panoramic vistas of snow-crowned Himalayan peaks, sparkling glacial river valleys, and remote mountain hamlets steeped in centuries-old traditions. The journey commences from Yuksom, taking explorers deep into untamed valleys where pleasant days with freezing nights and spectacular alpine weather. graces the trails. Each step along this route reveals untouched flora, alpine meadows, and timeless folklore cherished by the local indigenous communities.

Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Goechala - Dzongri Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.', 'The Goechala - Dzongri Trek is one of the most breathtaking Himalayan journeys situated across the mesmerizing landscapes of West Sikkim, Sikkim. Rising to an impressive altitude of 16100 ft over a duration of 11D/10N, this expedition offers a transcendent blend of ancient cultural lore, sacred alpine sanctuaries, and pristine high-altitude wilderness.

Traversing through dense oak, pine, and vibrant rhododendron canopies, travelers experience panoramic vistas of snow-crowned Himalayan peaks, sparkling glacial river valleys, and remote mountain hamlets steeped in centuries-old traditions. The journey commences from Yuksom, taking explorers deep into untamed valleys where pleasant days with freezing nights and spectacular alpine weather. graces the trails. Each step along this route reveals untouched flora, alpine meadows, and timeless folklore cherished by the local indigenous communities.

Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Goechala - Dzongri Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.',
        '[{"day": 1, "title": "NJP/Bagdogra to Yuksom", "description": "Day 1: NJP/Bagdogra to Yuksom (5,840 ft) \u2013 Drive approximately 150 km in 7\u20138 hours from NJP Railway Station or Bagdogra Airport to Yuksom, the historic gateway to the trek. The scenic journey passes through tea gardens, river valleys, and mountain roads before reaching the quaint Himalayan village. Overnight stay in a guesthouse.", "distance": "150 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 2, "title": "Yuksom to Sachen", "description": "Day 2: Yuksom to Sachen (7,200 ft) \u2013 Trek around 8 km in 5\u20136 hours through dense forests of oak, pine, and magnolia. Cross several suspension bridges over the Prek Chu River and follow a gradual ascent through lush woodland before reaching the peaceful campsite at Sachen. Overnight stay in tents.", "distance": "8 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 3, "title": "Sachen to Tshoka", "description": "Day 3: Sachen to Tshoka (9,700 ft) \u2013 Cover approximately 8 km in 5\u20136 hours while ascending through Bakhim and vibrant rhododendron forests. The trail offers occasional views of snow-covered peaks before arriving at the beautiful Tibetan settlement of Tshoka. Overnight stay in tents.", "distance": "8 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 4, "title": "Tshoka to Dzongri", "description": "Day 4: Tshoka to Dzongri (13,200 ft) \u2013 Trek nearly 9 km in 6\u20137 hours through rhododendron forests, alpine landscapes, and Deorali Top. As altitude increases, magnificent views of Kanchenjunga, Pandim, Kabru, and Rathong become visible. Reach Dzongri by evening and camp amidst stunning Himalayan scenery. Overnight stay in tents.", "distance": "9 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 5, "title": "Acclimatization at Dzongri", "description": "Day 5: Acclimatization at Dzongri (13,200 ft) \u2013 Spend the day acclimatizing with a short hike of about 2 km to Dzongri Top (13,800 ft). Witness a breathtaking sunrise over Kanchenjunga and the surrounding Himalayan peaks before returning to camp. The remainder of the day is reserved for rest and acclimatization. Overnight stay in tents.", "distance": "2 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 6, "title": "Dzongri to Thansing", "description": "Day 6: Dzongri to Thansing (12,900 ft) \u2013 Trek approximately 10 km in 5\u20136 hours across open alpine meadows and ridgelines. Descend towards Kokchurung and continue alongside the Prek Chu River to reach the picturesque campsite at Thansing, offering spectacular views of Mt. Pandim. Overnight camping.", "distance": "10 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 7, "title": "Thansing to Lamuney", "description": "Day 7: Thansing to Lamuney (13,600 ft) \u2013 Cover nearly 4 km in 2\u20133 hours through glacial valleys and high-altitude grasslands. This relatively short trekking day allows additional acclimatization and time to enjoy the pristine mountain environment. Overnight stay in tents at Lamuney.", "distance": "4 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 8, "title": "Lamuney to Goechala View Point", "description": "Day 8: Lamuney to Goechala View Point (15,100 ft) and Return to Thansing \u2013 Begin before sunrise and trek approximately 12\u201314 km in 8\u201310 hours. Pass the pristine Samiti Lake and ascend to Goechala View Point for spectacular close-up views of Kanchenjunga and neighboring peaks. After spending time at the viewpoint, descend back to Thansing for an overnight stay in tents.", "distance": "12\u201314 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 9, "title": "Thansing to Tshoka", "description": "Day 9: Thansing to Tshoka (9,700 ft) \u2013 Descend around 19 km in 7\u20138 hours via Kokchurung and Dzongri meadows before re-entering the rhododendron forests. The trail offers beautiful views of valleys, rivers, and alpine landscapes before reaching Tshoka. Overnight stay in tents.", "distance": "19 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 10, "title": "Tshoka to Yuksom", "description": "Day 10: Tshoka to Yuksom (5,840 ft) \u2013 Trek approximately 16 km in 6\u20137 hours through Bakhim and Sachen, crossing suspension bridges and forested sections before arriving back at Yuksom. Celebrate the completion of the trek and enjoy a comfortable overnight stay in a guesthouse.", "distance": "16 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 11, "title": "Yuksom to NJP/Bagdogra", "description": "Day 11: Yuksom to NJP/Bagdogra \u2013 Drive nearly 150 km in 7\u20138 hours back to NJP Railway Station or Bagdogra Airport. Enjoy the final views of Sikkim''s lush valleys and mountain scenery as the memorable Goechala\u2013Dzongri Trek concludes.", "distance": "150 km", "time": "", "image": ""}]'::jsonb, '[{"location": "Airport: Bagdogra Airport", "price": 0}, {"location": "Railway: New Jalpaiguri Railway Station", "price": 0}, {"location": "Base: Yuksom", "price": 0}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb,
