Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Singalila Pass Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.', 'The Singalila Pass Trek is one of the most breathtaking Himalayan journeys situated across the mesmerizing landscapes of West Sikkim, Sikkim. Rising to an impressive altitude of 11900 ft over a duration of 8D/7N, this expedition offers a transcendent blend of ancient cultural lore, sacred alpine sanctuaries, and pristine high-altitude wilderness.

Traversing through dense oak, pine, and vibrant rhododendron canopies, travelers experience panoramic vistas of snow-crowned Himalayan peaks, sparkling glacial river valleys, and remote mountain hamlets steeped in centuries-old traditions. The journey commences from Manebhanjan, taking explorers deep into untamed valleys where pleasant days, misty mornings and chilly nights. graces the trails. Each step along this route reveals untouched flora, alpine meadows, and timeless folklore cherished by the local indigenous communities.

Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Singalila Pass Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.',
        '[{"day": 1, "title": "NJP/Bagdogra to Dhotrey", "description": "Day 1: NJP/Bagdogra to Dhotrey (8,500 ft) \u2013 Drive approximately 95 km in 4\u20135 hours from NJP Railway Station or Bagdogra Airport to Dhotrey, a picturesque village near the Indo\u2013Nepal border. The route passes through Darjeeling''s tea gardens and mountain roads before reaching the trailhead. Overnight stay in a homestay or lodge.", "distance": "95 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 2, "title": "Dhotrey to Tonglu", "description": "Day 2: Dhotrey to Tonglu (10,130 ft) \u2013 Trek around 11 km in 5\u20136 hours through dense forests of rhododendron, bamboo, and magnolia. The gradual ascent offers beautiful views of the surrounding valleys and Himalayan ranges before reaching Tonglu, one of the highest points along the Singalila Ridge. Overnight stay in a trekkers'' hut or lodge.", "distance": "11 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 3, "title": "Tonglu to Kalipokhri", "description": "Day 3: Tonglu to Kalipokhri (10,400 ft) \u2013 Cover approximately 15 km in 6\u20137 hours along the Singalila Ridge, passing through Tumling, Gairibas, and Kaiyakatta. The trail provides magnificent views of Kanchenjunga and the Eastern Himalayas before arriving at the sacred black lake of Kalipokhri. Overnight stay in a lodge.", "distance": "15 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 4, "title": "Kalipokhri to Sandakphu", "description": "Day 4: Kalipokhri to Sandakphu (11,930 ft) \u2013 Trek nearly 6 km in 3\u20134 hours, ascending steadily towards Sandakphu, the highest point in West Bengal. Upon reaching the summit, enjoy spectacular panoramic views of Kanchenjunga, Everest, Lhotse, and Makalu stretching across the Himalayan skyline. Overnight stay in a lodge.", "distance": "6 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 5, "title": "Sandakphu to Phalut", "description": "Day 5: Sandakphu to Phalut (11,800 ft) \u2013 Trek approximately 21 km in 7\u20138 hours along the scenic Singalila Ridge. The trail remains largely undulating and offers uninterrupted views of the Kanchenjunga massif and surrounding peaks before reaching the remote campsite of Phalut. Overnight stay in a trekkers'' hut.", "distance": "21 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 6, "title": "Phalut to Gorkhey", "description": "Day 6: Phalut to Gorkhey (7,900 ft) \u2013 Descend around 15 km in 6\u20137 hours through dense forests of pine, oak, and rhododendron. The trail gradually loses altitude and leads to the peaceful village of Gorkhey, situated beside a mountain stream amidst lush greenery. Overnight stay in a homestay.", "distance": "15 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 7, "title": "Gorkhey to Srikhola", "description": "Day 7: Gorkhey to Srikhola (6,500 ft) and Drive to Darjeeling \u2013 Trek approximately 8 km in 3\u20134 hours through forest trails and small Himalayan villages to reach Srikhola. From here, drive nearly 50 km in 3\u20134 hours to Darjeeling, enjoying scenic mountain views along the way. Overnight stay in a hotel.", "distance": "50 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 8, "title": "Darjeeling to NJP/Bagdogra", "description": "Day 8: Darjeeling to NJP/Bagdogra \u2013 Drive approximately 75 km in 3\u20134 hours from Darjeeling to NJP Railway Station or Bagdogra Airport. The journey marks the conclusion of the Singalila Pass Trek, leaving behind unforgettable memories of the Eastern Himalayas and the majestic Sleeping Buddha range.", "distance": "75 km", "time": "", "image": ""}]'::jsonb, '[{"location": "Airport: Bagdogra Airport", "price": 0}, {"location": "Railway: New Jalpaiguri Railway Station", "price": 0}, {"location": "Base: Manebhanjan", "price": 0}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb,
