Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Sandakphu Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.',
        '[{"day": 1, "title": "NJP/Bagdogra to Sepi", "description": "Day 1: NJP/Bagdogra to Sepi (6,400 ft) and Trek to Gurdum (8,000 ft) \u2013 Drive approximately 95 km in 4\u20135 hours from NJP Railway Station or Bagdogra Airport to Sepi and begin the trek towards Gurdum. Cover around 10 km in 5\u20136 hours through dense forests of oak, bamboo, and rhododendron before reaching the tranquil village of Gurdum. Overnight stay in a homestay or lodge.", "distance": "10 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 2, "title": "Gurdum to Sandakphu", "description": "Day 2: Gurdum to Sandakphu (11,930 ft) \u2013 Trek nearly 13 km in 6\u20137 hours through steep forest trails and scenic ridges. As you gain altitude, breathtaking views of the Kanchenjunga massif begin to appear. Reach Sandakphu, the highest point in West Bengal, and witness stunning panoramas of Everest, Lhotse, Makalu, and Kanchenjunga. Overnight stay in a lodge.", "distance": "13 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 3, "title": "Sandakphu to Phalut", "description": "Day 3: Sandakphu to Phalut (11,800 ft) \u2013 Cover approximately 21 km in 7\u20138 hours along the picturesque Singalila Ridge. The trail offers uninterrupted views of the Himalayan giants and passes through alpine meadows before reaching the remote settlement of Phalut. Overnight stay in a trekkers'' hut or lodge.", "distance": "21 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 4, "title": "Phalut to Gorkhey", "description": "Day 4: Phalut to Gorkhey (7,900 ft) \u2013 Descend around 15 km in 6\u20137 hours through dense forests of pine, fir, and rhododendron. The route gradually drops in elevation and leads to the beautiful village of Gorkhey, nestled beside a mountain stream amidst lush greenery. Overnight stay in a homestay.", "distance": "15 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 5, "title": "Gorkhey to Srikhola", "description": "Day 5: Gorkhey to Srikhola (6,500 ft) and Drive to Darjeeling \u2013 Trek approximately 8 km in 3\u20134 hours through forested trails and small Himalayan hamlets to reach Srikhola. From here, drive nearly 50 km in 3\u20134 hours to Darjeeling, enjoying scenic mountain landscapes and tea gardens along the route. Overnight stay in a hotel.", "distance": "50 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 6, "title": "Darjeeling to NJP/Bagdogra", "description": "Day 6: Darjeeling to NJP/Bagdogra \u2013 Drive approximately 75 km in 3\u20134 hours from Darjeeling to NJP Railway Station or Bagdogra Airport. The journey concludes with lasting memories of the spectacular Himalayan vistas, charming villages, and iconic ridgelines of the Sandakphu Trek.", "distance": "75 km", "time": "", "image": ""}]'::jsonb, '[{"location": "Airport: Bagdogra Airport", "price": 0}, {"location": "Railway: New Jalpaiguri Railway Station", "price": 0}, {"location": "Base: Manebhanjan", "price": 0}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb,
        30.7333, 76.7794, '11930 ft', '', '',
        '{"Ideal Season": "Apr-Jun, Sep-Nov | Temp: -5\u2103'' to 20\u2103'' | Weather: Pleasant weather with cool breeze and panoramic Himalayan views."}'::jsonb, 'Apr-Jun, Sep-Nov', '287 km', 'Manebhanjan', 'Manebhanjan',
        'Bagdogra Airport', 'New Jalpaiguri Railway Station', 'Yes', '7000 ft', '11930 ft',
        '-5℃''', '20℃''', 'Pleasant weather with cool breeze and panoramic Himalayan views.', 'Sikkim', 'West Sikkim',
        'TREK', 5.0
    ) RETURNING id INTO tid;
    INSERT INTO public.trip_packages (trip_id, name, price, description, gst_percent) VALUES (tid, 'Standard Package', 16000.0, 'Standard booking package for Sandakphu Trek', 5.0);
    -- [Green Lake Trek]
    INSERT INTO public.trips (
        title, location, duration, difficulty, altitude, base_price, discount_percent, rating,
        image_url, images, category, description, trip_story, itinerary, pickup_options, inclusions,
        exclusions, carry_list, latitude, longitude, peak_elevation, trail_type, orientation,
        seasonal_info, best_months, total_distance, start_point, end_point, airport, railway,
        buses_cabs, min_height, max_height, min_temp, max_temp, weather, state, district,
        package_type, gst_percent
    ) VALUES (
        'Green Lake Trek', 'West Sikkim, Sikkim', '11D/10N', 'Moderate', '16500 ft', 50000.0, 0, 5.0,
        'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506744038136-46273834b3fb', '["https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506744038136-46273834b3fb"]'::jsonb,
        'Adventure', 'The Green Lake Trek is one of the most breathtaking Himalayan journeys situated across the mesmerizing landscapes of West Sikkim, Sikkim. Rising to an impressive altitude of 16500 ft over a duration of 11D/10N, this expedition offers a transcendent blend of ancient cultural lore, sacred alpine sanctuaries, and pristine high-altitude wilderness.

Traversing through dense oak, pine, and vibrant rhododendron canopies, travelers experience panoramic vistas of snow-crowned Himalayan peaks, sparkling glacial river valleys, and remote mountain hamlets steeped in centuries-old traditions. The journey commences from Gangtok, taking explorers deep into untamed valleys where cold alpine weather with pleasant days and freezing nights. graces the trails. Each step along this route reveals untouched flora, alpine meadows, and timeless folklore cherished by the local indigenous communities.

Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Green Lake Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.', 'The Green Lake Trek is one of the most breathtaking Himalayan journeys situated across the mesmerizing landscapes of West Sikkim, Sikkim. Rising to an impressive altitude of 16500 ft over a duration of 11D/10N, this expedition offers a transcendent blend of ancient cultural lore, sacred alpine sanctuaries, and pristine high-altitude wilderness.

Traversing through dense oak, pine, and vibrant rhododendron canopies, travelers experience panoramic vistas of snow-crowned Himalayan peaks, sparkling glacial river valleys, and remote mountain hamlets steeped in centuries-old traditions. The journey commences from Gangtok, taking explorers deep into untamed valleys where cold alpine weather with pleasant days and freezing nights. graces the trails. Each step along this route reveals untouched flora, alpine meadows, and timeless folklore cherished by the local indigenous communities.

Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Green Lake Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.',
        '[{"day": 1, "title": "NJP/Bagdogra to Lachen", "description": "Day 1: NJP/Bagdogra to Lachen (8,800 ft) \u2013 Drive approximately 130 km in 7\u20138 hours from NJP Railway Station or Bagdogra Airport to Lachen, passing through scenic valleys, waterfalls, and mountain roads of North Sikkim. Reach the beautiful mountain village by evening, complete permit formalities, and settle into a guesthouse for an overnight stay.", "distance": "130 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 2, "title": "Lachen to Zema", "description": "Day 2: Lachen to Zema (9,500 ft) and Trek to Talem (10,500 ft) \u2013 Drive for about 1 hour to Zema and begin the trek towards Talem. Cover nearly 10 km in 5\u20136 hours through dense forests of pine, fir, and rhododendron while following the course of the Zemu Chu River. Overnight stay in tents.", "distance": "10 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 3, "title": "Talem to Jakthang", "description": "Day 3: Talem to Jakthang (11,800 ft) \u2013 Trek approximately 11 km in 5\u20136 hours through alpine forests and open meadows. The trail gradually gains altitude, offering spectacular views of the surrounding ridges and valleys before reaching the campsite at Jakthang. Overnight camping.", "distance": "11 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 4, "title": "Jakthang to Yabuk", "description": "Day 4: Jakthang to Yabuk (13,100 ft) \u2013 Cover around 10 km in 5\u20136 hours while trekking through high-altitude meadows and glacial terrain. As vegetation becomes sparse, magnificent views of snow-clad peaks begin to emerge, creating a dramatic Himalayan landscape. Overnight stay in tents.", "distance": "10 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 5, "title": "Yabuk to Rest Camp", "description": "Day 5: Yabuk to Rest Camp (14,000 ft) \u2013 Trek nearly 8 km in 4\u20135 hours along the rugged Zemu Valley. The trail follows moraines and alpine stretches with increasingly impressive views of the Kanchenjunga massif and surrounding peaks. Overnight camping at Rest Camp.", "distance": "8 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 6, "title": "Rest Camp to Green Lake", "description": "Day 6: Rest Camp to Green Lake (16,200 ft) \u2013 Cover approximately 7 km in 4\u20135 hours through glacial terrain and rocky landscapes. Arrive at Green Lake, situated at the base of the mighty Kanchenjunga, and enjoy breathtaking panoramic views of the eastern Himalayan giants. Overnight stay in tents.", "distance": "7 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 7, "title": "Exploration and Acclimatization at Green Lake", "description": "Day 7: Exploration and Acclimatization at Green Lake (16,200 ft) \u2013 Spend the day exploring the surroundings of Green Lake and acclimatizing to the high altitude. Witness unparalleled views of Kanchenjunga, Siniolchu, Twin Peaks, and other snow-covered summits while enjoying the pristine wilderness of the Zemu Glacier region. Overnight camping.", "distance": "", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 8, "title": "Green Lake to Yabuk", "description": "Day 8: Green Lake to Yabuk (13,100 ft) \u2013 Descend approximately 15 km in 6\u20137 hours, retracing the route through glacial valleys and alpine meadows. Enjoy changing perspectives of the Himalayan landscape while returning to the familiar campsite at Yabuk. Overnight stay in tents.", "distance": "15 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 9, "title": "Yabuk to Talem", "description": "Day 9: Yabuk to Talem (10,500 ft) \u2013 Trek around 21 km in 7\u20138 hours through forests, river crossings, and scenic valleys. The long descent provides opportunities to observe the rich flora and fauna of North Sikkim before reaching Talem. Overnight camping.", "distance": "21 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 10, "title": "Talem to Zema and Drive to Lachen", "description": "Day 10: Talem to Zema and Drive to Lachen (8,800 ft) \u2013 Cover approximately 10 km in 4\u20135 hours while descending through dense forests to Zema. From here, drive for about an hour back to Lachen and enjoy a comfortable overnight stay in a guesthouse.", "distance": "10 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 11, "title": "Lachen to NJP/Bagdogra", "description": "Day 11: Lachen to NJP/Bagdogra \u2013 Drive nearly 130 km in 7\u20138 hours back to NJP Railway Station or Bagdogra Airport, passing through picturesque valleys and mountain roads. The journey marks the end of the spectacular Green Lake Trek, leaving unforgettable memories of one of Sikkim''s most remote and scenic adventures.", "distance": "130 km", "time": "", "image": ""}]'::jsonb, '[{"location": "Airport: Bagdogra Airport", "price": 0}, {"location": "Railway: New Jalpaiguri Railway Station", "price": 0}, {"location": "Base: Gangtok", "price": 0}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb,
        30.7333, 76.7794, '16500 ft', '', '',
        '{"Ideal Season": "Apr-Jun, Sep-Nov | Temp: -5\u2103'' to 20\u2103'' | Weather: Cold alpine weather with pleasant days and freezing nights."}'::jsonb, 'Apr-Jun, Sep-Nov', '352 km', 'Gangtok', 'Gangtok',
        'Bagdogra Airport', 'New Jalpaiguri Railway Station', 'Yes', '5800 ft', '16500 ft',
        '-5℃''', '20℃''', 'Cold alpine weather with pleasant days and freezing nights.', 'Sikkim', 'West Sikkim',
        'TREK', 5.0
    ) RETURNING id INTO tid;
    INSERT INTO public.trip_packages (trip_id, name, price, description, gst_percent) VALUES (tid, 'Standard Package', 50000.0, 'Standard booking package for Green Lake Trek', 5.0);
    -- [Kanchenjunga Base Camp Trek]
    INSERT INTO public.trips (
        title, location, duration, difficulty, altitude, base_price, discount_percent, rating,
        image_url, images, category, description, trip_story, itinerary, pickup_options, inclusions,
        exclusions, carry_list, latitude, longitude, peak_elevation, trail_type, orientation,
        seasonal_info, best_months, total_distance, start_point, end_point, airport, railway,
        buses_cabs, min_height, max_height, min_temp, max_temp, weather, state, district,
        package_type, gst_percent
    ) VALUES (
        'Kanchenjunga Base Camp Trek', 'West Sikkim, Sikkim', '13D/12N', 'Moderate', '16800 ft', 38000.0, 0, 5.0,
        'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506744038136-46273834b3fb', '["https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506744038136-46273834b3fb"]'::jsonb,
        'Adventure', 'The Kanchenjunga Base Camp Trek is one of the most breathtaking Himalayan journeys situated across the mesmerizing landscapes of West Sikkim, Sikkim. Rising to an impressive altitude of 16800 ft over a duration of 13D/12N, this expedition offers a transcendent blend of ancient cultural lore, sacred alpine sanctuaries, and pristine high-altitude wilderness.

Traversing through dense oak, pine, and vibrant rhododendron canopies, travelers experience panoramic vistas of snow-crowned Himalayan peaks, sparkling glacial river valleys, and remote mountain hamlets steeped in centuries-old traditions. The journey commences from Yuksom, taking explorers deep into untamed valleys where cold mountain climate with chilly winds and freezing nights. graces the trails. Each step along this route reveals untouched flora, alpine meadows, and timeless folklore cherished by the local indigenous communities.

Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Kanchenjunga Base Camp Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.', 'The Kanchenjunga Base Camp Trek is one of the most breathtaking Himalayan journeys situated across the mesmerizing landscapes of West Sikkim, Sikkim. Rising to an impressive altitude of 16800 ft over a duration of 13D/12N, this expedition offers a transcendent blend of ancient cultural lore, sacred alpine sanctuaries, and pristine high-altitude wilderness.

Traversing through dense oak, pine, and vibrant rhododendron canopies, travelers experience panoramic vistas of snow-crowned Himalayan peaks, sparkling glacial river valleys, and remote mountain hamlets steeped in centuries-old traditions. The journey commences from Yuksom, taking explorers deep into untamed valleys where cold mountain climate with chilly winds and freezing nights. graces the trails. Each step along this route reveals untouched flora, alpine meadows, and timeless folklore cherished by the local indigenous communities.

Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Kanchenjunga Base Camp Trek stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.',
        '[{"day": 1, "title": "NJP/Bagdogra to Yuksom", "description": "Day 1: NJP/Bagdogra to Yuksom (5,840 ft) \u2013 Drive approximately 150 km in 7\u20138 hours from NJP Railway Station or Bagdogra Airport to Yuksom, the historic gateway to western Sikkim. The scenic journey passes through river valleys, tea gardens, and mountain roads before reaching the picturesque village. Overnight stay in a guesthouse.", "distance": "150 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 2, "title": "Yuksom to Sachen", "description": "Day 2: Yuksom to Sachen (7,200 ft) \u2013 Trek around 8 km in 5\u20136 hours through dense forests of oak, pine, and magnolia. Cross several suspension bridges over the Prek Chu River and gradually ascend through lush woodland trails before reaching the peaceful campsite at Sachen. Overnight stay in tents.", "distance": "8 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 3, "title": "Sachen to Tshoka", "description": "Day 3: Sachen to Tshoka (9,700 ft) \u2013 Cover approximately 8 km in 5\u20136 hours while trekking through Bakhim and beautiful rhododendron forests. The trail steadily gains altitude and offers glimpses of snow-clad peaks before reaching the charming Tibetan settlement of Tshoka. Overnight stay in tents.", "distance": "8 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 4, "title": "Tshoka to Dzongri", "description": "Day 4: Tshoka to Dzongri (13,200 ft) \u2013 Trek nearly 9 km in 6\u20137 hours through rhododendron forests, alpine terrain, and Deorali Top. Spectacular views of Kanchenjunga, Pandim, Kabru, and Rathong begin to unfold as you approach Dzongri. Overnight camping amidst magnificent Himalayan scenery.", "distance": "9 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 5, "title": "Acclimatization at Dzongri", "description": "Day 5: Acclimatization at Dzongri (13,200 ft) \u2013 Spend the day acclimatizing with a short hike of about 2 km to Dzongri Top (13,800 ft). Witness a breathtaking sunrise over Kanchenjunga and surrounding peaks before returning to camp for rest and acclimatization. Overnight stay in tents.", "distance": "2 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 6, "title": "Dzongri to Thansing", "description": "Day 6: Dzongri to Thansing (12,900 ft) \u2013 Trek approximately 10 km in 5\u20136 hours across alpine meadows and ridgelines. Descend towards Kokchurung and continue alongside the Prek Chu River before reaching the scenic campsite at Thansing beneath the towering Mt. Pandim. Overnight camping.", "distance": "10 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 7, "title": "Thansing to Lamuney", "description": "Day 7: Thansing to Lamuney (13,600 ft) \u2013 Cover around 4 km in 2\u20133 hours through open grasslands and glacial valleys. The relatively short trek allows additional time for acclimatization and enjoying the stunning mountain environment surrounding Lamuney. Overnight stay in tents.", "distance": "4 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 8, "title": "Lamuney to Goechala View Point", "description": "Day 8: Lamuney to Goechala View Point (15,100 ft) and Return to Thansing \u2013 Begin before sunrise and trek approximately 12\u201314 km in 8\u201310 hours. Pass the pristine Samiti Lake and ascend to Goechala View Point, offering extraordinary close-up views of Kanchenjunga and its neighboring peaks. Descend back to Thansing for an overnight stay in tents.", "distance": "12\u201314 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 9, "title": "Thansing to Dzongri", "description": "Day 9: Thansing to Dzongri (13,200 ft) \u2013 Trek nearly 10 km in 5\u20136 hours while retracing the route through Kokchurung and alpine meadows. Enjoy changing perspectives of the Himalayan landscape before arriving back at Dzongri for the night. Overnight camping.", "distance": "10 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 10, "title": "Dzongri to Tshoka", "description": "Day 10: Dzongri to Tshoka (9,700 ft) \u2013 Descend approximately 9 km in 4\u20135 hours through rhododendron forests and mountain trails. Reach Tshoka by afternoon and spend the evening enjoying the serene atmosphere of this high-altitude settlement. Overnight stay in tents.", "distance": "9 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 11, "title": "Tshoka to Yuksom", "description": "Day 11: Tshoka to Yuksom (5,840 ft) \u2013 Trek around 16 km in 6\u20137 hours through Bakhim and Sachen, crossing suspension bridges and forested paths alongside the Prek Chu River before returning to Yuksom. Overnight stay in a guesthouse.", "distance": "16 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 12, "title": "Reserve Day for Weather or Exploration at Yuksom", "description": "Day 12: Reserve Day for Weather or Exploration at Yuksom \u2013 This day is kept as a contingency for adverse weather conditions, delayed movement at higher camps, or additional exploration around Yuksom. It provides flexibility for a safer and more comfortable trekking experience. Overnight stay in a guesthouse.", "distance": "", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 13, "title": "Yuksom to NJP/Bagdogra", "description": "Day 13: Yuksom to NJP/Bagdogra \u2013 Drive approximately 150 km in 7\u20138 hours back to NJP Railway Station or Bagdogra Airport, concluding the Kanchenjunga Base Camp Trek with unforgettable memories of the majestic Eastern Himalayas.", "distance": "150 km", "time": "", "image": ""}]'::jsonb, '[{"location": "Airport: Bagdogra Airport", "price": 0}, {"location": "Railway: New Jalpaiguri Railway Station", "price": 0}, {"location": "Base: Yuksom", "price": 0}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb,
        30.7333, 76.7794, '16800 ft', '', '',
        '{"Ideal Season": "Apr-Jun, Sep-Nov | Temp: -5\u2103'' to 20\u2103'' | Weather: Cold mountain climate with chilly winds and freezing nights."}'::jsonb, 'Apr-Jun, Sep-Nov', '389 km', 'Yuksom', 'Yuksom',
        'Bagdogra Airport', 'New Jalpaiguri Railway Station', 'Yes', '5800 ft', '16800 ft',
        '-5℃''', '20℃''', 'Cold mountain climate with chilly winds and freezing nights.', 'Sikkim', 'West Sikkim',
        'TREK', 5.0
    ) RETURNING id INTO tid;
    INSERT INTO public.trip_packages (trip_id, name, price, description, gst_percent) VALUES (tid, 'Standard Package', 38000.0, 'Standard booking package for Kanchenjunga Base Camp Trek', 5.0);
