Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Kasturi Peak TREK stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.', 'The Kasturi Peak TREK is one of the most breathtaking Himalayan journeys situated across the mesmerizing landscapes of West Sikkim, Sikkim. Rising to an impressive altitude of 16500 ft over a duration of 9D/8N, this expedition offers a transcendent blend of ancient cultural lore, sacred alpine sanctuaries, and pristine high-altitude wilderness.

Traversing through dense oak, pine, and vibrant rhododendron canopies, travelers experience panoramic vistas of snow-crowned Himalayan peaks, sparkling glacial river valleys, and remote mountain hamlets steeped in centuries-old traditions. The journey commences from Yuksom, taking explorers deep into untamed valleys where cold alpine weather with freezing nights and strong winds near the summit. graces the trails. Each step along this route reveals untouched flora, alpine meadows, and timeless folklore cherished by the local indigenous communities.

Whether ascending dramatic ridge lines, camping beneath star-studded Himalayan skies, or immersing in the spiritual resonance of the high Himalayas, the Kasturi Peak TREK stands as an unforgettable expedition of exploration, resilience, and natural majesty.',
        '[{"day": 1, "title": "Day 1", "description": "Day 1: Arrive at Yuksom and complete trek formalities before spending the day acclimatizing in this historic gateway to the Kanchenjunga region. Explore the local monastery and surrounding forests before an overnight stay at Yuksom. Altitude: 1,780 m.", "distance": "", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 2, "title": "Day 2", "description": "Day 2: Begin the trek from Yuksom to Sachen through dense forests of oak, chestnut and rhododendron, crossing several suspension bridges over the Prek Chu River. The trail gradually ascends and takes around 5\u20136 hours to cover approximately 8 km. Overnight stay at Sachen. Distance: 8 km | Duration: 5\u20136 hours.**", "distance": "8 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 3, "title": "Day 3", "description": "Day 3: Trek from Sachen to Tshoka, passing through Bakhim and beautiful rhododendron forests. The trail becomes steeper as it climbs toward the traditional Tibetan settlement of Tshoka. The trek covers about 7 km and takes 4\u20135 hours. Overnight stay at Tshoka. Distance: 7 km | Duration: 4\u20135 hours.**", "distance": "7 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 4, "title": "Day 4", "description": "Day 4: Continue trekking from Tshoka to Dzongri through alpine meadows and rhododendron forests, gradually gaining altitude with magnificent mountain views unfolding along the way. Cover approximately 10 km in 5\u20136 hours and camp at Dzongri. Distance: 10 km | Duration: 5\u20136 hours.**", "distance": "10 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 5, "title": "Day 5", "description": "Day 5: Spend the day acclimatizing at Dzongri with an excursion to Dzongri Top for panoramic views of Kanchenjunga, Kabru, Pandim and other Himalayan peaks. Return to camp for rest and acclimatization. Duration: 3\u20134 hours.**", "distance": "", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 6, "title": "Day 6", "description": "Day 6: Trek from Dzongri to Kasturi Peak Base Camp, traversing high-altitude meadows, moraines and glacial terrain with spectacular views of the surrounding mountains. Cover around 8 km in 5\u20136 hours before establishing camp near the base of Kasturi Peak. Distance: 8 km | Duration: 5\u20136 hours.**", "distance": "8 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 7, "title": "Day 7", "description": "Day 7: Attempt Kasturi Peak and return to base camp. The summit climb involves steep ascents over rocky and snow-covered terrain, rewarding trekkers with breathtaking views of the Kanchenjunga massif and surrounding Himalayan ranges. The day''s trek takes approximately 8\u201310 hours. Duration: 8\u201310 hours.**", "distance": "", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 8, "title": "Day 8", "description": "Day 8: Descend from Kasturi Peak Base Camp to Tshoka via Dzongri, retracing the scenic route through alpine landscapes and rhododendron forests. Cover around 18 km in 7\u20138 hours before an overnight stay at Tshoka. Distance: 18 km | Duration: 7\u20138 hours.**", "distance": "18 km", "time": "", "image": ""}, {"day": 9, "title": "Day 9", "description": "Day 9: Trek down from Tshoka to Yuksom through Bakhim and Sachen, enjoying the final views of the dense Himalayan forests. The descent covers approximately 15 km and takes 6\u20137 hours, marking the end of the Kasturi Peak Trek. Distance: 15 km | Duration: 6\u20137 hours.**", "distance": "15 km", "time": "", "image": ""}]'::jsonb, '[{"location": "Airport: Bagdogra Airport", "price": 0}, {"location": "Railway: New Jalpaiguri Railway Station", "price": 0}, {"location": "Base: Yuksom", "price": 0}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb,
